cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this plugin in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "LandXML Road & Terrain GIS Tools"
abstract: >-
  A QGIS Processing plugin that brings LandXML road and terrain data from
  Civil 3D, OpenRoads and other design software into QGIS. It imports TIN
  surfaces, breaklines, alignments with true arc-length stationing,
  vertical and existing-ground profiles and corridor cross-sections;
  computes cut/fill and corridor earthworks quantities; produces
  cross-section sheets and road design reports; and runs a geometric
  design review (alignment phasing, sight distance, vertical and
  horizontal curves, grades, superelevation and barrier warrants) against
  Kenya RDM 1.3 (2025) or AASHTO 2018 criteria, writing recommended PVIs
  back for Civil 3D. It needs no Python packages beyond those shipped with
  QGIS.
